  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.ahsme-1981-p15.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(A=\\log_b2,\\) \\(B=\\log_b3,\\) and \\(u=\\log_bx.\\) Taking base-\\(b\\) logarithms gives \\(A(A+u)=B(B+u).\\) Since \\(A\\ne B,\\) \\[ A+B+u=0. \\] Therefore \\(u=-\\log_b6=\\log_b(\\frac{1}{6}),\\) so \\(x=\\frac{1}{6}.\\)\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is B.",
      "hints": [
        "Take logarithms to base \\(b\\) of the two equal positive powers",
        "Let \\(A=\\log_b2,\\) \\(B=\\log_b3,\\) and \\(u=\\log_bx\\)"
      ],
